## How It Works

A 2MB arena is divided into 64-byte blocks, yielding 32768 blocks. The free list is a single atomic head packed into a 64-bit value: [ version (upper 32 bits) | head index (lower 32 bits) ]. A free block stores the index of the next free block. On init, all blocks form a chain starting at 0, ending with a sentinel (0xFFFFFFFF).

The allocator uses a lock-free approach:
- Alloc: read the head with acquire, compute the next pointer, CAS to update head to next and increment version. Return the block corresponding to the popped index.
- Free: write the freed block’s next pointer to current head, CAS to push it back and increment version.

ABA is mitigated by the version counter; each successful CAS increments the version, so a stale head cannot be mistaken for a newer one.

Memory order choices:
- Loads use memory_order_acquire to synchronize with the producer/consumer.
- Stores use memory_order_release or memory_order_acq_rel to ensure visibility of the updated head and block linkage.

### Key Points
- **64-bit head encoding**: version guards against ABA by differentiating sequential head values.
- **Block linkage stored in arena**: next indices reside in the block headers themselves.
- **Initialization**: pre-link 32768 blocks and set head to 0 with version 1.
- **Threading model**: works with many producers/consumers with minimal contention due to CAS on a single head.

### Example
```c
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stddef.h>

#define ARENA_SIZE (2*1024*1024)
#define BLOCK_SIZE 64
#define BLOCKS (ARENA_SIZE / BLOCK_SIZE)

typedef struct { uint32_t next; } Block;
static uint8_t arena[ARENA_SIZE];
static _Atomic uint64_t head; // [version:upper32 | index:lower32]

static inline void init_slab(void) {
  for (uint32_t i = 0; i < BLOCKS-1; ++i) ((Block*)arena)[i].next = i+1;
  ((Block*)arena)[BLOCKS-1].next = 0xFFFFFFFFu;
  atomic_store_explicit(&head, ((uint64_t)1 << 32) | 0u, memory_order_relaxed);
}

void* slab_alloc(void) {
  uint64_t oldv, newv;
  uint32_t idx, ver, next;
  while (1) {
    oldv = atomic_load_explicit(&head, memory_order_acquire);
    idx = (uint32_t)(oldv & 0xFFFFFFFFu);
    ver = (uint32_t)(oldv >> 32);
    if (idx == 0xFFFFFFFFu) return NULL;
    next = ((Block*)arena)[idx].next;
    newv = ((uint64_t)(ver+1) << 32) | (uint64_t)next;
    if (atomic_compare_exchange_weak_explicit(&head, &oldv, newv,
                                            memory_order_acquire, memory_order_relaxed))
      return (void*)(arena + (size_t)idx * BLOCK_SIZE);
  }
}

void slab_free(void* p) {
  if (!p) return;
  uint32_t idx = ((uint8_t*)p - arena) / BLOCK_SIZE;
  uint64_t oldv, newv;
  while (1) {
    oldv = atomic_load_explicit(&head, memory_order_acquire);
    uint32_t ver = (uint32_t)(oldv >> 32);
    ((Block*)arena)[idx].next = (uint32_t)(oldv & 0xFFFFFFFFu);
    newv = ((uint64_t)(ver+1) << 32) | idx;
    if (atomic_compare_exchange_weak_explicit(&head, &oldv, newv,
                                            memory_order_release, memory_order_relaxed))
      break;
  }
}

